        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "badge_number": "02",
            "category": "Products & Technology",
            "question": "How does Lumina Europa differ from a traditional tissue mask?",
            "answer": "<p> Traditional sheet masks are usually made from fabric or serum-soaked hydrogel. Lumina nanofiber masks use an extremely fine fiber structure, designed to perfectly mold to the natural contour of the face. This creates a completely different application experience and allows the active formula to be delivered without the heavy, wet feel of a conventional mask. </p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "badge_number": "03",
            "category": "Products & Technology",
            "question": "What are nanofibers?",
            "answer": "<p> Nanofibers are exceptionally fine fibers created using specialized manufacturing technologies. Their small diameter allows them to form a light and highly adaptable structure that sits perfectly on the surface of the skin. </p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "badge_number": "04",
            "category": "Products & Technology",
            "question": "Does \"nanofiber\" mean the product contains nanoparticles?",
            "answer": "<p> Not necessarily. \"Nanofiber\" describes the physical structure of the fiber material. It should not be construed to mean that every ingredient in the formulation is a nanomaterial or a nanoparticle. </p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "badge_number": "05",
            "category": "Products & Technology",
            "question": "How does the nanofiber mask work?",
            "answer": "<p> When the mask is activated as directed, the nanofiber structure interacts with moisture and allows the formula contained in the fibers to transfer to the skin. </p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "badge_number": "06",
            "category": "Products & Technology",
            "question": "Why is close skin contact important?",
            "answer": "<p> The skin is not perfectly flat. The fine structure of the fibers can follow its natural contour much more closely, helping to ensure more even contact between the mask and the skin's surface. </p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
